## 6. Depth & Elevation

AutoLeap uses a **restrained shadow system**. Shadows are functional (they communicate hierarchy), never decorative.

| Level | CSS | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| Flat | No shadow | Inline elements, text, icons |
| Subtle | `shadow-xs` | Buttons, inputs, chips — slight lift |
| Low | `shadow-sm` | Cards, containers — primary content surfaces |
| Medium | `shadow-md` | Dropdowns, popovers — interactive overlays |
| High | `shadow-lg` | Modals, command palettes — focus-stealing surfaces |
| Highest | `shadow-xl` | Full-screen overlays, dialogs |

**Rules:**
- Never combine border AND shadow on the same element. Pick one.
- Dark mode: Shadows become less visible. Use border (Navy 600) as the primary depth signal.
- No colored shadows. No blur > 24px. No spread > 4px.

