## 7. Do's and Don'ts

### Do

- ✅ Use `rounded-lg` (8px) on ALL buttons — consistent with cards and inputs
- ✅ Apply the raised gradient + inset highlight treatment on all filled/solid buttons
- ✅ Keep flat treatment (no gradient, no shadow) on dim/outline/ghost variants
- ✅ Use Menlo exclusively for machine-generated data
- ✅ Keep icon stroke width at exactly 1.5px — never the default 2px
- ✅ Land all spacing on the 4px grid
- ✅ Use Slate scale for all neutrals
- ✅ Add visible focus rings on every interactive element
- ✅ Keep transitions under 200ms for a snappy enterprise feel
- ✅ Use Navy surfaces for dark mode — not pure black
- ✅ Reserve Gold for premium, high-signal moments only
- ✅ Add tooltips to every icon-only button

### Don't

- ❌ Use gray, zinc, stone, or neutral Tailwind scales — Slate only
- ❌ Apply heavy shadows (`shadow-lg`+) to cards — save those for modals
- ❌ Use Menlo for headings, labels, buttons, or navigation
- ❌ Exceed 1.5px stroke width on Lucide icons
- ❌ Add decorative elements or illustrations
- ❌ Use `rounded-full` on buttons — that's only for badges, tabs, and pills
- ❌ Create buttons with `rounded-md` (6px) or `rounded-xl` (12px) — always `rounded-lg` (8px)
- ❌ Apply the raised gradient treatment to dim, outline, or ghost buttons — those stay flat
- ❌ Use layout shifts on hover for flat buttons (scale, padding changes). Only filled buttons get the subtle translateY lift.
- ❌ Apply opacity below 0.3 for disabled states (use 0.5)
- ❌ Mix font families within a single data context

